PARITY (web BulkActionsToolbar.tsx → native — every branch + t() call reproduced)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Withdrawn: web `count === 0 → return null` → native `.isWithdrawn` renders EmptyView (the
    documented "mount unconditionally" pattern; peer of the AiUsageCard off-mode gate — NOT a
    hidden section).
  • Active bar: GlassPanel (→ tsGlassPanel) sticky row, role=region aria-label
    "Bulk actions for selected items"; accent count chip ("{count} selected", aria-live polite →
    `updatesFrequently`); optional itemNoun (one/other) + "of {total}" (shown only when itemNoun
    set AND total is a number — incl. the web's computed-but-unshown `bulk.itemDefault` default).
  • Actions: variant danger→.destructive else .secondary, optional SF Symbol, loading=pending
    (TSButton spinner), disabled=disabled||pending; ghost Clear button. flex-wrap → ViewThatFits
    (single row / stacked).
  • runAction: pending double-fire guard; confirm gate via the native useConfirm peer
    (BulkActionsConfirmPresenter + native .alert, destructive role); !ok → abort; throw leaves the
    selection intact → P4 leaf retry affordance (+ warning glyph + VoiceOver hint).
  • Empty-actions: a friendly caption renders so the active bar is never a blank box.
  • All 5 web t() keys (bulk.selected/itemDefault/ofTotal/toolbarLabel/clear) + 4 native-chrome
    keys promoted to the P1/S10 "BulkActionsToolbar" .strings table; no English literals in code.
  • a11y: per-element VoiceOver labels (chip summary, each action incl. failed-retry, Clear);
    Dynamic Type (Font.TS system ramp); reduce-motion respected (TSFadeIn).
  • view.opened (P1/S11) emitted once, deferred past the withdrawn state.

